# One line-ending policy, in the repo instead of in every clone's autocrlf.
#
# Without this, a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` reports files "modified"
# with an empty diff whenever a tool writes LF into the working tree — the
# content is identical, only the ending differs, and the phantom reappears
# every time git touches the file. Normalising to LF everywhere ends the whole
# class: every tool in this repo (cargo, node, vite, python) is happy with LF
# on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one thing that genuinely wants CRLF; PowerShell does not, but
# keeping scripts it owns in its native ending costs nothing.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touched: content-addressed or binary.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.onnx binary
